            "review_text": "De…Niiiiccccee\nSingapore, Singapore85 contributions\n0\nGreat local food as a baseline to compare.food standards\nOct 2013 • Couples\nThis restaurant was introduced by the hotel for good local food. We went there twice as we liked the food there compared to what we had elsewhere. Great variety and choice of local dishes and fragrant lemongrass flavoured rice served in individual claypots. The local grill meats and seafood are a must try and the vegetables are fresh! Morning glory or kangkong is known as bindweed here and I prefer the varietal here compared to other Asean countries. The grilled plain squid is delicious and the beef is very flavourful. Price is more expensive than most places but worth the extra buck.\nRead more\nWritten November 18, 2013",
